{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":392,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"“My spirit is consumed. My days are extinct and the grave is ready for me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1235},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":393,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"Surely there are mockers with me. My eye dwells on their provocation.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1239},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":394,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"“Now give a pledge. Be collateral for me with yourself. Who is there who will strike hands with me?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1243},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":395,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"For you have hidden their heart from understanding, therefore you will not exalt them.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1246},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":396,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"He who denounces his friends for plunder, even the eyes of his children will fail.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1249},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":397,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"“But he has made me a byword of the people. They spit in my face.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1253},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":398,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"My eye also is dim by reason of sorrow. All my members are as a shadow.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1256},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":399,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"Upright men will be astonished at this. The innocent will stir himself up against the godless.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1259},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":400,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"Yet the righteous will hold to his way. He who has clean hands will grow stronger and stronger.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1262},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":401,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"But as for you all, come back. I will not find a wise man among you.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1265},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":402,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"My days are past. My plans are broken off, as are the thoughts of my heart.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1268},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":403,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"They change the night into day, saying ‘The light is near’ in the presence of darkness.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1272},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":404,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"If I look for Sheol as my house, if I have spread my couch in the darkness,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1275},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":405,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"if I have said to corruption, ‘You are my father,’ and to the worm, ‘My mother,’ and ‘My sister,’","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1278},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":406,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"where then is my hope? As for my hope, who will see it?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1281},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":17,"verse_ordinal":407,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"Shall it go down with me to the gates of Sheol, or descend together into the dust?”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1284}]}